 "goal": "Crouch through an attack as you come in, and punish it before the attacker can act",
 "why": "A hit taken crouching has two thirds of its knockback, and with the stick held down {char} is back on the floor as its freeze ends, while the attacker is still in its move. Coming into an opponent's reach crouching turns its attack into {char}'s punish. It holds until the damage is high enough that the hit knocks {char} down all the same.",
 "switch": "success",
 "shield": "infinite",
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "Come into the opponent's reach and hold the stick down before it attacks. Keep it down through the hit's freeze: {char} stays on the floor. Then the C-stick down, A or Z.",
  "expect": "The opponent plays footsies and attacks when {char} comes in. A try begins when its attack hits and is judged when {char}'s punish lands or the opponent can act again: whether {char} was crouching, stayed on the floor, and punished.",
