  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: {opp}'s {move} hits {char}, crouching. The freeze"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "Crouch cancel",
    "text": [
     "A hit taken crouching has two thirds of its knockback, and freezes {char} two thirds as long.",
     "With the stick still down when the freeze ends, {char} stays on the floor, or is put back on it at once. Taken standing, the same hit sends {char} away in hitstun."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         "SPEED",
         0
        ],
        "frame": "WALK",
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 600,
        "from": {
         "near": "NEAR"
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: {opp}'s {move} hits {char}, standing"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "Coming in",
    "text": [
     "{opp} keeps its distance and attacks when {char} comes into its reach. There is no time to see the attack and crouch: the stick goes down as {char} arrives, before it.",
     "A walk stops into a crouch at once. A dash does not: let go of the stick first."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         "SPEED",
         0
        ],
        "frame": "WALK",
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 600,
        "from": {
         "near": "NEAR"
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: {opp}'s {move} hits {char}, crouching. The freeze"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         1,
         8
        ],
        "words": "Crouching: keep the stick down",
        "kind": "go"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "The punish",
    "text": [
     "The attacker is still in its move when {char} can act again, a few frames after the freeze.",
     "The C-stick down is a down smash, A with the stick still down a down tilt, Z a grab. Which reaches depends on where the attack left the attacker: a dash attack often ends on top of {char}, or past."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         "SPEED",
         0
        ],
        "frame": "WALK",
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 600,
        "from": {
         "near": "NEAR"
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: {opp}'s {move} hits {char}, crouching. The freeze"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         1,
         8
        ],
        "words": "Crouching: keep the stick down",
        "kind": "go"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "On the floor",
    "text": [
     "An opponent that misses its tech lies on the floor until it chooses how to get up. Its getup attack hits on both sides, but weakly.",
     "Standing over it crouching covers that choice: the attack is crouch cancelled, and it is open for as long as the attack lasts. It pushes {char} back a little: the punish has to reach."
    ],
    "scenario": 5,
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         "SPEED",
         0
        ],
        "frame": "WALK",
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 600,
        "from": {
         "near": "NEAR"
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: {opp}'s {move} hits {char}, crouching. The freeze"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         1,
         8
        ],
        "words": "Crouching: keep the stick down",
        "kind": "go"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "Where it stops",
    "text": [
     "Knockback grows with damage. Once two thirds of it still sends {char} tumbling, crouching no longer holds: {char} is knocked down.",
     "Here, at {PCT}%, {opp}'s {move} does that. From there on the answer is the shield, or staying out of reach."
    ],
    "scenario": 12,
    "show": {
     "example": {
